---
import MemberLayout from "../../layouts/MemberLayout.astro";
const version = Date.now();

const frontmatter = {
  title: "Withdraw Credits Securely | Wikimint Marketing Platform",
  description:
    "Request credit withdrawals through the Wikimint Marketing Platform. Review your available withdrawal balance, manage payment methods, track withdrawal history, and monitor the status of every withdrawal request from one convenient page.",
  image:
    "/assets/images/others/withdraw-credits-wikimint-marketing-platform.webp",
  tags: ["about", "business", "finance"],
  author: "Wikimint Team",
  disableAds: true,
};
---

<MemberLayout frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <div class="mo mb-10">
    <section id="walletSummary" class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border p-6">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Available Credits</div>

        <div id="availableCredits" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">0</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border p-6">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Pending Withdrawals</div>

        <div id="pendingWithdrawals" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">0</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border p-6">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Withdrawable Credits</div>

        <div
          id="withdrawableCredits"
          class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-green-600">
          0
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="paymentMethodCard" class="mt-8 rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Payment Method</h2>

          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
            Withdrawals will be sent to this account.
          </p>
        </div>

        <button id="editPaymentMethod" type="button" class="btn-ol">
          Add / Edit
        </button>
      </div>

      <div id="paymentMethodContent" class="mt-6">Loading...</div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Request Withdrawal</h2>

      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500">
        Withdraw your available credits using your saved payment method.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <label class="mb-2 block text-sm font-medium"> Credits </label>

        <input
          id="withdrawCredits"
          type="number"
          min="0"
          step="0.000001"
          class="w-full rounded-lg border p-3"
        />
      </div>

      <div id="withdrawInfo" class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500"></div>

      <button id="requestWithdrawal" class="btn mt-6">
        Request Withdrawal
      </button>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Withdrawal History</h2>

      <div id="withdrawalHistory" class="mt-6">Loading...</div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <article class="prose lg:prose-xl max-w-none">
    <h1>Withdraw Your Credits | Wikimint Marketing Platform</h1>

    <p>
      The Withdrawals page allows eligible members to request credit withdrawals
      from their account using their preferred payment method. It provides a
      simple place to review your available withdrawal balance, submit new
      requests, and monitor the status of previous withdrawals.
    </p>

    <button class="w-full btn login go"> Promote Your Personal Brand </button>

    <img
      loading="lazy"
      src="/assets/images/others/withdraw-credits-wikimint-marketing-platform.webp"
      alt="Modern illustration representing secure credit withdrawals, digital payments, account balance, payment methods, withdrawal history, and member earnings on the Wikimint Marketing Platform."
      title="Withdraw Credits | Wikimint Marketing Platform"
      class="w-full"
    />

    <p>
      Every withdrawal request is reviewed according to the platform rules
      before payment is processed. This helps maintain a fair payment system for
      every member while protecting the platform from invalid or duplicate
      requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Submit Withdrawal Requests with Confidence</h2>

    <p>
      When your account becomes eligible, you can request a withdrawal directly
      from this page.
    </p>

    <p>Before submitting a request, review:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Your available withdrawal balance</li>
      <li>Minimum withdrawal amount</li>
      <li>Saved payment method</li>
      <li>Requested withdrawal amount</li>
      <li>Withdrawal history</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Checking these details helps reduce delays during the review process.</p>

    <h2>Save Your Preferred Payment Method</h2>

    <p>
      Your payment information can be saved securely in your account so you do
      not need to enter it every time you request a withdrawal.
    </p>

    <p>
      If your payment details change in the future, simply update them before
      submitting your next request.
    </p>

    <h2>Track Every Withdrawal Request</h2>

    <p>
      Every request progresses through different stages before payment is
      completed.
    </p>

    <p></p>Depending on its current status, your request may appear as:

    <ul>
      <li>Pending</li>
      <li>Approved</li>
      <li>Paid</li>
      <li>Cancelled</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Your withdrawal history allows you to review previous requests whenever
      needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Available Balance and Pending Requests</h2>

    <p>
      The amount available for withdrawal is calculated according to your
      eligible credit balance and any withdrawal requests that are still waiting
      to be processed.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you already have a pending request, the available balance shown on this
      page automatically reflects that amount until the request has been
      completed or cancelled.
    </p>

    <h2>Review Your Withdrawal History</h2>

    <p>
      Keeping a record of previous requests makes it easier to track payments
      over time.
    </p>

    <p>
      Your withdrawal history provides useful information such as request dates,
      requested amounts, payment status, and completed payments.
    </p>

    <h2>Before You Submit a Request</h2>

    <p>
      Taking a few moments to review your account can help avoid unnecessary
      delays.
    </p>

    <p>Confirm that:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Your payment method is correct.</li>
      <li>Your withdrawal amount meets the minimum requirement.</li>
      <li>Your available balance is sufficient.</li>
      <li>Your account information is current.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Accurate information allows the review process to move forward more
      efficiently.
    </p>

    <h2>A Simple Payment Experience</h2>

    <p>
      The Withdrawals page is designed to make requesting payments
      straightforward for eligible members.
    </p>

    <p>
      From checking your available balance to reviewing payment history, every
      important detail is available in one place, allowing you to manage your
      withdrawal requests with confidence while keeping a complete record of
      your account activity.
    </p>

    <section id="faq" class="hr bg-white">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="acc space-y-4">
        <div class="space-y-4" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q1" checked />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q1" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  How do I request a withdrawal on the Wikimint Marketing
                  Platform?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  Eligible members can submit a withdrawal request from the
                  Withdrawals page after meeting the platform requirements.
                  Before sending your request, review your available withdrawal
                  balance, verify your saved payment method, and enter the
                  amount you wish to withdraw. Once submitted, your request will
                  appear in your withdrawal history until processing has been
                  completed.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q2" />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q2" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  When can I submit a withdrawal request?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  You can submit a withdrawal request after your account has
                  sufficient eligible credits available for withdrawal and any
                  applicable minimum withdrawal requirement has been met. The
                  Withdrawals page displays your available withdrawal balance,
                  helping you determine whether your account is currently ready
                  for a new withdrawal request.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q3" />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q3" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  Why is my available withdrawal balance different from my total
                  credit balance?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  Not every credit shown in your account is immediately
                  available for withdrawal. Your available withdrawal balance is
                  calculated according to the platform rules and may also take
                  pending withdrawal requests into account. This provides an
                  accurate view of the amount that can currently be requested.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q4" />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q4" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  What payment methods are supported?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  The Wikimint Marketing Platform supports approved payment
                  methods that are available within your account settings. You
                  can save your preferred payment information in advance, making
                  future withdrawal requests faster and more convenient. If your
                  payment details change, simply update them before submitting
                  another request.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q5" />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q5" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  Can I change my payment information after submitting a
                  withdrawal request?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  If you need to change your payment information after
                  submitting a request, update your saved payment method as soon
                  as possible. Depending on the processing stage of your
                  request, you may also need to contact platform support.
                  Keeping your payment details current helps reduce unnecessary
                  processing delays.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="acc-item">
            <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q6" />
            <div
              itemprop="mainEntity"
              itemscope
              itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
              <label for="q6" class="acc-title">
                <h3 itemprop="name" class="text-lg">
                  How can I check the status of my withdrawal request?
                </h3>
              </label>
              <div
                itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                itemscope
                itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
                class="acc-content">
                <p itemprop="text">
                  Every withdrawal request appears in your withdrawal history
                  together with its current processing status. Depending on
                  where it is in the review process, the status may show as
                  Pending, Approved, Paid, or Cancelled. Reviewing your history
                  allows you to follow the progress of each request from
                  submission through completion.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="acc-item">
          <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q7" />
          <label for="q7" class="acc-title">
            <h3 class="text-lg">Why is my withdrawal request still pending?</h3>
          </label>
          <div class="acc-content">
            <p>
              Every withdrawal request is reviewed before payment is completed.
              Processing time may vary depending on account verification,
              payment schedules, request volume, or other platform checks. A
              Pending status simply means your request is waiting to complete
              the normal review and payment process.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="acc-item">
          <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q8" />
          <label for="q8" class="acc-title">
            <h3 class="text-lg">
              Can I submit multiple withdrawal requests at the same time?
            </h3>
          </label>
          <div class="acc-content">
            <p>
              The platform may limit additional requests while an earlier
              withdrawal is still waiting for processing. This helps maintain
              accurate account balances and avoids duplicate payment requests.
              Review your withdrawal history before creating another request to
              confirm whether an existing request is still pending.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="acc-item">
          <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q9" />
          <label for="q9" class="acc-title">
            <h3 class="text-lg">
              What should I check before requesting a withdrawal?
            </h3>
          </label>
          <div class="acc-content">
            <p>
              Before submitting a request, confirm that your payment information
              is correct, your available withdrawal balance is sufficient, and
              the requested amount meets the published withdrawal requirements.
              Spending a few moments reviewing these details helps avoid
              unnecessary corrections after your request has been submitted.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="acc-item">
          <input type="radio" name="acc" id="q10" />
          <label for="q10" class="acc-title">
            <h3 class="text-lg">Where can I view my previous withdrawals?</h3>
          </label>
          <div class="acc-content">
            <p>
              Your complete withdrawal history is available on the Withdrawals
              page. Each record shows useful information such as the request
              date, requested amount, payment method, processing status, and
              completed payments. This history provides a convenient record for
              reviewing your account activity whenever needed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</MemberLayout>

<script
  is:inline
  type="module"
  src={`/assets/js/withdrawals.js?v=${version}`}
  defer></script>
